abstract:
Of the infinitely many lines that separate two classes, one is best: the one furthest from both. This topic builds the maximal-margin classifier from geometry — functional versus geometric margin, why maximising $2/\|w\|$ becomes minimising $\frac12\|w\|^2$, the constrained optimisation, the Lagrangian dual, KKT conditions, and why only the support vectors matter. It also shows exactly where the hard margin breaks, which motivates Topics 73 and 74.}
